      "role": "user",
      "content": "wireshark... okay. i'll look into it. but it's just so overwhelming. like, does this kind of thing happen in these types of sociological experiments? i've read some theories online that they use low-frequency signals or subtle digital pulses to keep subjects in a state of mild anxiety so they can track stress responses. does that sound like something they would actually do to keep people under observation?",
